        <implementation markdown="Single tumor cells or small cluster of tumor cells, not larger than 0.2 mm in diameter, usually detected by immunohistochemistry or molecular pathology. No typical characteristics of metastases (stromal reaction, proliferation).&#xA;If such ITC are detected in lymph nodes, those are classified as pN0(i+) or pN0(mol+) (regional) or as pM0(i+) or pM0(mol+) (non-regional).&#xA;For negativity of immunohistochemical or molecular pathologic findings in lymph nodes the same rules are applied (i- or mol-)"/>
        <name language="de-DE" lastTranslated="2017-06-30T17:53:44">isolierte Tumorzellen</name>
        <desc language="de-DE" lastTranslated="2017-06-30T17:54:27">weniger als 200 metastatische Tumorzellen (Gesamtdurchmesser unter 200 Mikrometer.</desc>
